    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b2ffd489-b2a5-5ccf-9a23-8b5f7250d8f8" activityNameId="70e625f5-5c29-584f-8878-dfaeaa585a33" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Lignite briquettes, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Lignite briquettes, at plant
Low heating value is 19.5 MJ/kg. Bulk density is 730 kg/m3. No details on the production process are available. Emission data from drying and milling available from references. The emitted trace elements are proportional to the trace elements in the lignite. Losses from the prozess (0.5 %) are accounted as lignite ashes. The energy requirements are from an onsite mine-mouth lignite power plant.;
UUID: 721546ff-94ea-3d7b-a501-4b7fc3cb1ae5
The water content of the lignite is reduced in driers from initial 60 % to 20 %. Production of briquettes and lignite dust follows. 
Location: German conditions.
Technology: Details not available.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography/Text
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_721546ff-94ea-3d7b-a501-4b7fc3cb1ae5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
